2:T761,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest way to remodel a kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping the existing layout and refreshing sound cabinets, handles, lighting, paint, flooring or the splashback can be more economical than moving services or replacing every unit. The best option depends on the kitchen's condition."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I remodel a kitchen without replacing the cabinets?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. If the cabinet boxes are sound and the layout works, you may be able to replace or repaint the doors, add new handles, renew plinths and fit a new worktop. Proper preparation is important for a durable result."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a kitchen remodel on a budget cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Costs vary widely. A cosmetic refresh is typically less than a full refit, but room size, materials, appliance work, access, labour and hidden repairs all affect the final price. Every project differs, so obtain a free, itemised quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes the biggest visual difference in a budget kitchen makeover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cabinet fronts, worktops, lighting and the overall colour scheme can have a major effect on appearance because they cover large or prominent areas. Neat finishing details, such as silicone, trims and aligned handles, also matter."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I keep the existing kitchen layout to save money?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. Keeping sinks, appliances and services in their current positions can reduce plumbing, electrical and flooring changes. However, a layout that wastes space or creates safety issues may justify additional work."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-remodel-on-a-budget-before-and-after","d"]
